.TH HYD 1 "2026-11-24" "hydd 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyd \- query and maintain a hydd Hydrus PTR mirror
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyd
.RI [ \-\-sha256 | \-\-sha1 | \-\-md5 ]
.I FILE
.br
.B hyd
.I HASH
.br
.B hyd
.B stats
.br
.B hyd
.B counts
.I TAG
.RI [ TAG ...]
.br
.B hyd
.B hashes
.RB [ \-\-offset
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-limit
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-after
.IR ID ]
.I TAG
.RI [ TAG ...]
.br
.B hyd
.B hashes\-after
.I TAG ID
.RI [ LIMIT ]
.br
.B hyd
.BR rebuild\-counts | check | scan | repair | verify | version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyd
is a small companion client for
.BR hydd (8).
It hashes a file or accepts a hash, asks the running local API for that file's
tags, prints derived tag statistics, and runs the maintenance commands that
operate on the store or the update cache.
.PP
Query commands use the local API, so the daemon must be running. Loopback
requests are trusted by default. If the daemon sets
.B require_localhost_key = true\fR,
run as the
.I hyd
user or set
.B HYDD_API_KEY
to a configured access key.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "hyd " FILE
Hash
.I FILE
with SHA-256 (the default) and print its storage and display tags. The output
starts with a comment line containing the file name, algorithm, and hash.
.TP
.BI "hyd " HASH
Query a 64-character SHA-256, 40-character SHA-1, or 32-character MD5 hash
directly. An argument that is both a valid hash and an existing file name is
rejected as ambiguous; write
.I ./FILE
to force the file interpretation.
.TP
.B hyd stats
Print repository statistics, sync state, live build progress, and an estimate
of when the next PTR update will be applied. Equivalent to
.BR "hydd \-\-stats" .
.TP
.BI "hyd counts " TAG ...
Ask the running API for the exact current mapping count of each storage tag.
One line of the form
.IR "TAG<TAB>COUNT"
is printed per tag. A tag that is not defined in the repository is reported
as unknown. This requires
.B tag_counts_enabled = true
(the default) and exits non-zero if any lookup fails.
.TP
.BI "hyd hashes " "[options] " TAG ...
Page the reverse tag index. Several tags are ANDed, and a tag beginning with
.B \-
is excluded (AND NOT). One SHA-256 hash is printed per line; page progress
goes to stderr. The options must come before the tags:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " " N
Start at page offset
.I N
(default 0, maximum 10000000).
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " " N
Page size, 1 to 1000 (default 100).
.TP
.BI \-\-after " " ID
Continue after the internal hash id
.I ID
from a previous response's
.IR next_after .
This is mutually exclusive with
.B \-\-offset
and has no depth cap.
.RE
.IP
Requires
.B tag_hashes_enabled = true
and
.B tag_counts_enabled = true
in the daemon configuration.
.TP
.BI "hyd hashes\-after " "TAG ID " [ LIMIT ]
Continue a single-tag reverse lookup after the
.I ID
returned as
.IR next_after .
.I LIMIT
defaults to 100.
.TP
.B hyd rebuild\-counts
Rebuild the derived
.I counts.bin
and
.I tag_lookup.bin
files and exit. This reads the live store and is CPU and I/O heavy on a full
mirror. If the data directory is root-owned, the command retries through
.B doas
or
.B sudo
when the first attempt looks like a permission or daemon-lock failure.
.TP
.B hyd check
Run
.B hydd \-\-verify\-store
followed by
.BR "hydd \-\-check\-tag\-counts" .
This validates the store and recounts the derived tag metadata without writing
anything. Run it while a compaction is not in flight for a guaranteed-consistent
result.
.TP
.B hyd scan
Parse every cached update file with the current importer and report files that
would make a sync fail. Equivalent to
.BR "hydd \-\-scan\-updates" .
.TP
.B hyd repair
Re-hash every update file referenced by the repository metadata and re-download
missing or corrupt entries. Requires
.B keep_update_cache = true
in the daemon configuration. Equivalent to
.BR "hydd \-\-repair\-cache" .
.TP
.B hyd verify
Open and validate the store and print its counts. Equivalent to
.BR "hydd \-\-verify\-store" .
.TP
.B hyd version
Print the daemon version in the form
.IR "hyd vX.Y.Z" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-sha256
Hash
.I FILE
with SHA-256. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-sha1
Hash
.I FILE
with SHA-1 for legacy lookups.
.TP
.B \-\-md5
Hash
.I FILE
with MD5 for legacy lookups.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Equivalent to
.BR "hyd version" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HYD_BIN
The
.B hydd
executable to run. Default:
.IR hydd .
.TP
.B HYD_CONFIG
The configuration file passed to
.BR hydd .
Default:
.IR /etc/hydd.conf .
.TP
.B HYDD_API_KEY
Access key used by
.B hydd \-\-stats
and the API-backed lookups against an instance that requires a key from
localhost.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hydd.conf
Default configuration file for the daemon.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hyd
Default data directory: store, delta journal, sync state, update cache, and
generated keys.
.SH EXAMPLES
Look up tags for a file:
.PP
.nf
    hyd photo.jpg
.fi
.PP
Query a hash directly:
.PP
.nf
    hyd 4c77267f93415de0bc33b7725b8c331a809a924084bee03ab2f5fae1c6019eb2
.fi
.PP
Count mappings for several tags:
.PP
.nf
    hyd counts "series:touhou" "character:reimu"
.fi
.PP
Page the files for a tag and continue from the cursor:
.PP
.nf
    hyd hashes --limit 1000 "series:touhou"
    hyd hashes-after "series:touhou" 123456 1000
.fi
.PP
Verify the store and the derived counts:
.PP
.nf
    hyd check
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success. Usage errors, failed lookups, and failed maintenance commands
return non-zero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hydd (8),
.BR hydd.conf (5),
.IR https://github.com/lusoterra/hyd .
